group: D2h
formula: C2H4
construction: two equivalent halves
headline: 
source: MO levels: RHF, 6-31G* · 
note: Model from extended Hückel (qualitative) · model energies in eV · calculation in Hartree · electrons: CH2 1 (neutral: 1 unpaired e), drawn 1; CH2 1 (neutral: 1 unpaired e), drawn 1; model and calculation: 2 drawn + 0 folded (0 levels) = 2 · labels in D<sub>2h</sub>
about: The extended Hückel diagram explains the calculation's orbitals: nothing more, nothing less.\n\n**The model.** Every column is extended Hückel (Alvarez parameters). The middle column is the molecule's own extended Hückel run, the side columns are the two fragments' (CH2 and CH2). The basis is the same in all three, so the lines are an exact projection of each model MO on the fragment orbitals: a line joins a model MO to a fragment level that makes up at least 10 % of it.\n\n**Bonding and antibonding** are read from the sign of each model MO's overlap population between the two fragments, then paired per symmetry label and degeneracy, so each antibonding level has its bonding partner; a level without a partner is non-bonding. Colours mark the pairs.\n\n**The calculation** is the column on the right, on its own energy axis in Hartree and to scale. For each model level it shows the calculated orbital (or set of near-degenerate orbitals) with the largest overlap with it, at its calculated energy, in the colour of the model level it matches. A level marked ≈ matches only loosely (overlap below 0.80; the value is in the hover text). Labels are those of the matched calculated orbital. Clicking a level shows that orbital in 3-D.\n\nThe model explains your occupied orbitals and the LUMO in the right order. Virtual orbitals above the LUMO depend strongly on the basis set.\n\n**Total electrons: 2** (CH2 1, CH2 1).\n\nEach model level carries a short grey tag naming the fragment orbitals it is mostly made of (shares of at least 20 %), such as Cr d or CO π*. Ligand-field view hides empty ligand-centred levels such as CO π*; transitions into them are charge transfer, not d–d.\n\n**Orbital labels.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D2h; the code reported none.  b1 and b2 (b2 and b3 in D2h) depend on the choice of axes; ECCE follows Mulliken's convention, as most textbooks do.
verdict: ok The model explains your occupied orbitals and the LUMO in the right order.
